1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:04,030
In Core, open the Records
navigation and choose Analytics.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,529
The selected Executive summary tab
gives the department's recorded summary.

3
00:00:08,859 --> 00:00:13,520
Start with From, To, Station
slash group and Definition.

4
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:17,479
This example displays August second
through October thirty-first,

5
00:00:17,709 --> 00:00:20,680
with All station groups and
All definitions selected.

6
00:00:21,129 --> 00:00:24,700
Read the Generated line and Records
read count with those filters.

7
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:29,000
The page says that dashboards are
computed on demand over finalized

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,659
Records, and that viewers see the
Records they are authorized to open.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,270
Your account's access and the
displayed reporting scope both

10
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:37,889
matter when comparing results.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,910
Scroll to Headline figures
and read the prior-period

12
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:42,900
dates before comparing values.

13
00:00:43,289 --> 00:00:48,829
Here, Records finalized is four, Personnel
hours and Training hours are each zero

14
00:00:48,829 --> 00:00:51,270
point five, and Amendments is one.

15
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:56,309
Incident reports, unit responses
and the NERIS counts are zero

16
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,610
in this fictional dataset.

17
00:00:58,079 --> 00:01:01,860
The values beneath the tiles show
their comparison with the prior period.

18
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:05,260
These are measures derived from
the saved software records.

19
00:01:05,569 --> 00:01:10,049
They do not independently confirm
physical attendance, service delivery or a

20
00:01:10,049 --> 00:01:12,439
department's real operational performance.

21
00:01:12,619 --> 00:01:17,940
Continue to Lifecycle, Queues and
obligations, By month and By definition.

22
00:01:18,469 --> 00:01:22,330
Median hours to finalize is zero
point one here, while several

23
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,259
unavailable measures show a dash.

24
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:26,749
A dash is not a measured zero.

25
00:01:27,219 --> 00:01:30,949
Open drafts shows one and
Awaiting review shows zero.

26
00:01:31,379 --> 00:01:35,279
Those are current visible-queue counts,
rather than the finalized-record

27
00:01:35,279 --> 00:01:37,010
count of a selected definition.

28
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:41,070
The breakdown tables show four
October records, split between

29
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:44,850
two Training records and two
community software-exercise records.

30
00:01:45,319 --> 00:01:49,530
Use the headings, counts, hours
and shares together to understand

31
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:51,140
what each panel is describing.

32
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:54,879
Return to the filter row and
select Training in Definition.

33
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,530
Before you choose Filter,
the earlier Generated line

34
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:00,689
still says Records read, four.

35
00:02:01,049 --> 00:02:05,149
This separates a prepared field selection
from refreshed dashboard output.

36
00:02:05,639 --> 00:02:09,310
Check the intended dates and group
at the same time, then choose

37
00:02:09,310 --> 00:02:11,200
Filter to request the new result.

38
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:14,839
Selecting a reporting filter
changes the question you ask of

39
00:02:14,839 --> 00:02:19,300
the saved data; it does not edit,
finalize or delete a record.

40
00:02:19,579 --> 00:02:24,039
After choosing Filter, read the returned
filter row and generated result.

41
00:02:24,469 --> 00:02:27,839
Training remains selected,
and Records read is now two.

42
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:30,940
The dates and All station
groups remain the same.

43
00:02:31,389 --> 00:02:35,919
This readback establishes which definition
subset the dashboard actually loaded.

44
00:02:36,319 --> 00:02:40,339
When comparing two views, verify
their returned selections and counts

45
00:02:40,339 --> 00:02:44,050
before attributing a difference to
changing activity in your department.

46
00:02:44,230 --> 00:02:46,400
Scroll to the refreshed headline figures.

47
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:50,759
Records finalized is now two,
while Training hours and Personnel

48
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:52,710
hours remain zero point five.

49
00:02:53,139 --> 00:02:57,220
The broader four-record view included
two community exercise records with

50
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:01,129
no recorded hours, so narrowing
to Training changes the count

51
00:03:01,170 --> 00:03:03,119
without changing these hour totals.

52
00:03:03,469 --> 00:03:04,869
Amendments remains one.

53
00:03:05,369 --> 00:03:09,869
Compare each named measure with its own
purpose rather than assuming every tile

54
00:03:09,869 --> 00:03:11,780
must change when a filter is applied.

55
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:16,289
Return to Station slash group,
select Engine fifty-one and choose

56
00:03:16,289 --> 00:03:18,570
Filter, keeping Training selected.

57
00:03:18,939 --> 00:03:21,690
The returned page says Records read, zero.

58
00:03:22,159 --> 00:03:25,899
Read that zero with the selected
group, definition, dates

59
00:03:25,999 --> 00:03:27,459
and your account's access.

60
00:03:27,739 --> 00:03:30,059
It describes this saved Records subset.

61
00:03:30,399 --> 00:03:34,579
It does not establish that the whole
department has no activity, that nobody

62
00:03:34,579 --> 00:03:39,129
attended training, or that records
outside your authorized view do not exist.

63
00:03:39,309 --> 00:03:43,790
In this filtered result, Records
finalized and Training hours are zero,

64
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:45,979
while Amendments still shows one.

65
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:50,300
For this department-administrator
account, that amendment figure counts

66
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:54,439
department transitions in the time
window; it is not the finalized-record

67
00:03:54,439 --> 00:03:55,890
count of the selected group.

68
00:03:56,329 --> 00:04:00,429
The empty breakdown panels say No
finalized Records in this window.

69
00:04:00,919 --> 00:04:05,380
Read the actual label and scope of each
measure before using it to explain a

70
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,700
change or assess a department's workload.

71
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:12,609
Select All station groups and All
definitions, then choose Filter again.

72
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:16,100
The returned Generated
line reads four records.

73
00:04:16,449 --> 00:04:20,400
This restores the broader reporting
scope without changing the saved records.

74
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:24,149
Recheck these selections whenever
you move between a narrowly scoped

75
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,290
question and a department-wide review.

76
00:04:26,659 --> 00:04:30,319
A useful comparison begins with
a deliberate, verified scope.

77
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:34,440
Choose the Workload tab for another
view of the same recorded activity.

78
00:04:34,829 --> 00:04:39,360
Recheck its date, group and definition
filters and the Generated count.

79
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:43,450
Here, it reads four records, with
zero point five Record hours,

80
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:45,799
Personnel hours and Training hours.

81
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:48,809
These headings describe different
measures even when their

82
00:04:48,809 --> 00:04:50,609
displayed values happen to match.

83
00:04:50,939 --> 00:04:54,650
Use this view to understand how
recorded work is distributed, while

84
00:04:54,650 --> 00:04:57,879
checking the underlying entries
when a result needs explanation.

85
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:01,109
Scroll to By month and By definition.

86
00:05:01,599 --> 00:05:05,279
October contains four records
and zero point five hours.

87
00:05:05,619 --> 00:05:09,850
In the definition table, Training
has two records, zero point five

88
00:05:09,899 --> 00:05:11,830
hours and a fifty-percent share.

89
00:05:12,159 --> 00:05:16,789
The community software-exercise definition
also has two records and a fifty-percent

90
00:05:16,789 --> 00:05:19,209
share, but zero recorded hours.

91
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:23,039
Equal record counts do not
mean equal recorded duration.

92
00:05:23,459 --> 00:05:26,879
Read all three columns before
deciding where more detail or a

93
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:28,729
closer records review is needed.

94
00:05:28,939 --> 00:05:33,550
Continue to Records by weekday
and hour, then the person, unit,

95
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,740
author and station-group panels.

96
00:05:36,249 --> 00:05:39,699
The matrix distributes these
recorded entries by their timestamps.

97
00:05:40,169 --> 00:05:44,910
By person shows Matthew Casey with
one entry and zero point five hours.

98
00:05:45,369 --> 00:05:48,439
By author shows Wallace
Boden with four records.

99
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:52,310
By station group separates
Command from Firehouse fifty-one.

100
00:05:52,929 --> 00:05:57,009
Participation, authorship and group
assignment answer different questions.

101
00:05:57,439 --> 00:06:00,589
The unit panel has no finalized
Records in this window.

102
00:06:01,089 --> 00:06:05,069
This fictional matrix is not a live
staffing display or independent

103
00:06:05,069 --> 00:06:06,940
evidence of current response demand.

104
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:10,639
Start with a reporting question that
matches your department's records.

105
00:06:10,989 --> 00:06:14,409
Community paramedicine and mental
health teams can review outreach

106
00:06:14,409 --> 00:06:18,069
documentation, search-and-rescue
teams can compare mission-support

107
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:22,640
records, security companies can
examine recorded service activity, and

108
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:26,829
wildland or industrial response teams
can review their own documented work.

109
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:31,439
Fire and EMS departments can use
the same filter and readback habits.

110
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:37,320
Choose the intended window, definition and
group, refresh the view, then investigate

111
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:41,550
the underlying records before drawing
conclusions from a count or hour total.

